## Incident Documentation

The following information is required to complete the timeline:

- Exact circumstances of the initial approach.
- Location and approximate time of the encounter, if appropriate to disclose.
- Identity or affiliation of the individual, if established and appropriate to document.
- Specific statements, questions, or requests made during the encounter.
- Whether sensitive or confidential information was requested or disclosed.
- Date and method of reporting.
- Any acknowledgment or response from safety personnel.
- Subsequent developments or organizational actions.

## Evidence and Verification

Each timeline entry should be supported by an appropriate source whenever possible.

Evidence may include:

- Original written communications.
- Contemporaneous notes.
- Emails and responses.
- Relevant documentation.
- Firsthand observations.

Unverified information will be clearly identified rather than presented as established fact.

## Timeline Limitations

This is a preliminary timeline. The exact sequence of events and reporting actions remains subject to verification against the original incident documentation.

No assumptions will be made about the individual's intent, organizational affiliation, or involvement in corporate espionage.

